<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibf6469f608857613d4d4ebfc226f98811e1d4c01" commit="34e247b370ffe8da98c0bbf0893e44174afb17d5" commit_message="cryptohome: Bind mount daemon store folders  Adds infrastructure that allows system daemons that run inside a mount namespace to 'see' their per-user daemon store folder in Cryptohome mounts. This is implemented in a way that only the daemon sees its own daemon store and nobody else's and other daemons do not see this daemon's store.  The first user is authpolicyd, which stores the user's Kerberos ticket in this folder, see CL:1113917.  See CL:1136440 resp. (once that CL lands) https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/docs/+/master/sandboxing.md for details.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:1169817  BUG=chromium:738433 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=amd64-generic --packages cryptohome      With the above authpolicy CL, log in to an Active Directory managed      device and check /home/root/&lt;user_hash&gt;/authpolicyd. A file should      appear there.  Change-Id: Ibf6469f608857613d4d4ebfc226f98811e1d4c01 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1127665 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1127665" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="14" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/65/1127665/14" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id9a6c86df6e5e27a3b816ab2f23f27ff659f5704" commit="1419800d33fcedd6b6c283417ff36ad8daafaba6" commit_message="platform_FilePerms: Handle /run/daemon-store  Whitelists /run/daemon-store and makes sure that all contained directories are root-owned with a corresponding directory in /etc/daemon-store. Cryptohome mounts the user's cryptohome into these daemon store directories. See CL:1136440 for details.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:1127665  BUG=chromium:738433 TEST=Ran test  Change-Id: Id9a6c86df6e5e27a3b816ab2f23f27ff659f5704 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1169817 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1169817" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/17/1169817/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0e8da2ff70069ad2548bd998b7a4d952e27b2d26" commit="d7ab32958055a6f0accecb9a38e2b490edd25f79" commit_message="cryptohome: Cleanup home and daemon directory mounts  This CL largely just shifts things around to deduplicate the code to mount user/root homes and daemon store folders. However, there are some subtle differences: - In the ephemeral case, the legacy home /home/chronos/user and   /home/chronos/u-&lt;user_hash&gt; are bound to   /run/cryptohome/ephemeral_mount/&lt;user_hash&gt; instead of   /home/user/&lt;user_hash&gt;. This is more in line with the non-ephemeral   case and shouldn't matter. - Errors out on MountLegacyHome() in non-ephemeral mode. The old code   wouldn't do that, but that looked like a bug. - RememberBind() and RememberMount() spit out errors now themselves, not   the calling functions (in most cases).  BUG=None TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=amd64-generic --packages cryptohome  Change-Id: I0e8da2ff70069ad2548bd998b7a4d952e27b2d26 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1143480 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ryo Hashimoto &lt;hashimoto@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1143480" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/80/1143480/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ice300a3e3896548d98daf917022d207537b3ab31" commit="954bc406a4c84539ca4e9aced1a2d3a179aad7f0" commit_message="Explicitly disable X11.  It is no longer necessary to maintain project-freon as a separate entity from the main overlay, so it is being merged into the defaults. This commit re-adds the freon setting that explicitly disables X11. The disable was previously removed along with the USE enabling X11, but that is not sufficient, it needs to be explicitly disabled.  BUG=chromium:730026 TEST=local builds, precq passes  Change-Id: Ice300a3e3896548d98daf917022d207537b3ab31 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1173411 Commit-Ready: Alex Klein &lt;saklein@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Klein &lt;saklein@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1173411" owner_email="saklein@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/11/1173411/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib0f815c3555f299083697c5adb600670069a1e8f" commit="3e7f92a263f2a7e82b15e2aca09b5b4e2700e11e" commit_message="Removed project-freon master and parent references.  It is no longer necessary to maintain project-freon as a separate entity from the main overlay, so it is being merged into the defaults. This commit removes instances of freon being referenced as a master or parent of an overlay.  BUG=chromium:730026 TEST=precq passes CQ-DEPEND=CL:1165329, CL:1165943, CL:1173411  Change-Id: Ib0f815c3555f299083697c5adb600670069a1e8f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1165961 Commit-Ready: Alex Klein &lt;saklein@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Klein &lt;saklein@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1165961" owner_email="saklein@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/61/1165961/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="19"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I84b6a14980cdf6df48c2b1a3c9e4577d0aae9ab6" commit="445df4830ed540dc703ab2aefdbdac880fad285a" commit_message="diagnostics: Add seccomp filters for diagnosticsd  Add seccomp filters that were collected after some ad-hoc manual testing on several test devices.  The filters are presumably enough for doing D-Bus and gRPC communication (both - client-sided and server-sided).  BUG=chromium:869377 TEST=start diagnosticsd under minijail with the filters and check      that it doesn't crash  Change-Id: I84b6a14980cdf6df48c2b1a3c9e4577d0aae9ab6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1167285 Commit-Ready: Maksim Ivanov &lt;emaxx@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Maksim Ivanov &lt;emaxx@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1167285" owner_email="emaxx@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/85/1167285/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7827999ebc5abd59f2487249f4b904319c84481c" commit="aa56136cd5eb038b700e241bd747f6c036f8901b" commit_message="login: Handle &quot;cleanup&quot; TPM firmware update mode  This adds a mode that allows Chrome to trigger cleanup, which boils down to a request to perform another TPM clear to flush out a vulnerable SRK.  BUG=chromium:872746 TEST=new unit tests 